    Call 1: ("In lcms/src/cmsio0.c, what is the best project-consistent way for _cmsReadHeader to validate type compatibility before setting TagLinked for two directory entries with identical offset and size? Please inspect relevant descriptor structures, helper declarations/order, plugin support, and upstream/history if recognizable. Should compatibility mean intersection of the two tag descriptors' SupportedTypes, or should the code read the shared on-disk base type and verify both descriptors support that exact type? Note that _cmsReadHeader is currently iterating the directory, so seeking into tag payload may disturb directory reading unless position is restored.", "The reported vulnerability is that _cmsReadHeader at lcms/src/cmsio0.c lines 795-803 links any same-offset/same-size entries without implementing its 'Check types' comment. A crafted desc then gamt pair shares an mft2 payload. cmsReadTag(gamt) resolves the link to the desc slot and stores a cmsPipeline there; SaveTags later uses the desc descriptor and treats it as cmsMLU, causing an ASan heap overflow. I have confirmed cmsReadTag checks the requested signature against the payload base type, but because _cmsSearchTag follows the link, the cooked pointer lands in the earlier signature's slot. We need fix root cause, likely only create links where tag descriptors are compatible, while preserving legitimate ICC shared tag data and behavior for unknown/plugin descriptors.")...
